cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: 'Solver, parameters and certificates for "New spherical codes by tuning an annealing solver"'
abstract: >-
  A solver for the spherical code problem: place N points on the unit sphere in R^D so that
  the smallest pairwise angle is as large as possible. It repeatedly anneals a LogSumExp
  surrogate of the largest pairwise cosine, minimizes it with L-BFGS-B and perturbs the points
  with Student-t noise between anneals. The repository contains the solver, one global
  parameter set, the parameters fitted separately for each of the 29,670 instances with
  3 <= D <= 32 and 2D < N <= 1024, and certificates for 24 exact codes.
